            Smart Scam Detector
        </h2>

        <p>
            Paste a suspicious message to get an educational risk check.
        </p>

    </div>


    <div class="checker card">

        <textarea
            id="scamText"
            placeholder="Paste a suspicious message here..."
        ></textarea>


        <button
            class="primary"
            id="scanBtn"
        >
            Analyze Message
        </button>


        <div
            id="scanResult"
            class="result"
        ></div>

    </div>

</section>


<!-- =========================================================
     URL CHECKER
     ========================================================= -->

<section id="url" class="page">

    <div class="page-title">

        <h2>
            Suspicious URL Checker
        </h2>

        <p>
            Basic browser-only checks for common warning signs.
        </p>

    </div>


    <div class="checker card">

        <input
            id="urlInput"
            placeholder="https://example.com"
        >


        <button
            class="primary"
            id="urlBtn"
        >
            Check URL
        </button>


        <div
            id="urlResult"
            class="result"
        ></div>

    </div>

</section>


<!-- =========================================================
     SOCIAL MEDIA SAFETY
     ========================================================= -->

<section id="social" class="page">

    <div class="page-title">

        <h2>
            Social Media Safety
        </h2>

        <p>
            Quick habits for safer social accounts.
        </p>

    </div>


    <div class="info-grid">

        <!-- 1. PRIVACY & PROFILE CONTROL -->
        <div class="info card scam-info-card">
            <div class="card-banner">
                <img src="images/social-privacy.svg" alt="Social Media Privacy Settings">
            </div>

            <span class="scam-tag red">ACCOUNT PRIVACY</span>

            <h3>Social Media Privacy &amp; Profile Control</h3>

            <p>
                By default, most social platforms (Instagram, Facebook, Snapchat, X) keep your account public. Anyone can see your friends list, posts, travel photos, family pictures, and tag you in malicious scams without your permission.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>🔒 <strong>Private Account:</strong> Switch personal profiles to "Private" so only people you explicitly approve can view your posts and stories.</li>
                <li>🚫 <strong>Hide Sensitive Details:</strong> Never display your phone number, personal email, home address, or birthday year publicly on your profile bio.</li>
                <li>👥 <strong>Story &amp; Post Audience:</strong> Utilize "Close Friends" features on Instagram or custom privacy lists on Facebook for personal family updates.</li>
                <li>🔍 <strong>Search &amp; Tagging Restrictions:</strong> Disable search engine indexing of your profile and require manual review for photo tags.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="how-protect">
                <b>Action Steps:</b> Go to Settings → Privacy → Account Privacy → Turn on "Private Account". Under "Tags &amp; Mentions", select "Don't allow tags" or require approval.
            </div>
        </div>


        <!-- 2. TWO-FACTOR AUTHENTICATION & LOGIN SECURITY -->
        <div class="info card scam-info-card">
            <div class="card-banner">
                <img src="images/social-security.svg" alt="Two-Factor Authentication Security">
            </div>

            <span class="scam-tag orange">LOGIN DEFENSE</span>

            <h3>2FA &amp; Account Takeover Prevention</h3>

            <p>
                Account hacking and takeover scams are surging. Scammers send phishing links like "Your copyright was violated" or "Someone is using your photos" to steal your password and lock you out permanently.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>🛡️ <strong>Enable Authenticator 2FA:</strong> Don't rely solely on SMS OTP (vulnerable to SIM swap). Use Google Authenticator, Authy, or Microsoft Authenticator.</li>
                <li>⚠️ <strong>Phishing Alerts:</strong> Platforms NEVER send direct messages (DMs) claiming copyright violations or asking for your password. Official notices appear in Settings.</li>
                <li>📱 <strong>Active Session Review:</strong> Regularly check "Where You're Logged In" in Settings and log out from unfamiliar devices or browsers immediately.</li>
                <li>🔑 <strong>Unique Passwords:</strong> Never use the same password for Instagram, email, and banking. A breach on one exposes all of them.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="how-protect">
                <b>Action Steps:</b> Go to Settings → Accounts Center → Password and Security → Two-Factor Authentication → Select Authenticator App and save backup codes safely.
            </div>
        </div>


        <!-- 3. FAKE ACCOUNTS & IMPERSONATION -->
        <div class="info card scam-info-card">
            <div class="card-banner">
                <img src="images/social-impersonation.svg" alt="Fake Accounts & Identity Theft">
            </div>

            <span class="scam-tag pink">IMPERSONATION &amp; CLONES</span>

            <h3>Fake Profiles, Cloning &amp; DM Scams</h3>

            <p>
                Cybercriminals frequently clone profiles by copying profile pictures and bios of your friends, then sending frantic messages like "My account got locked, please click this link" or "Can you lend me urgent money?".
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>🧐 <strong>Spot Cloned Accounts:</strong> Check the username carefully for subtle spelling changes (e.g., extra underscores, zero instead of letter 'O', or missing letters).</li>
                <li>📞 <strong>Verify Before Responding:</strong> If a friend contacts you from a "new account" asking for emergency funds, call them directly on their original number.</li>
                <li>🗳️ <strong>Voting &amp; Contest Scams:</strong> Never click on "Vote for my photography entry" or "Help me become an ambassador" links received in Instagram/Snapchat DMs.</li>
                <li>🚫 <strong>Report Immediately:</strong> Use the in-app "Report → Pretending to be someone I know" option so platform AI can remove the malicious clone.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="how-protect">
                <b>Action Steps:</b> Never send money or verification codes to ANY follower through DMs. Always report and block fraudulent clone accounts immediately.
            </div>
        </div>


        <!-- 4. DIGITAL FOOTPRINT & OVERSHARING -->
        <div class="info card scam-info-card">
            <div class="card-banner">
                <img src="images/social-footprint.svg" alt="Digital Footprint and Oversharing">
            </div>

            <span class="scam-tag yellow">DATA EXPOSURE</span>

            <h3>Digital Footprint &amp; Location Oversharing</h3>

            <p>
                Everything you upload creates a permanent digital footprint. Burglars and stalkers exploit live check-ins, while identity thieves collect pieces of your identity from daily stories and photo metadata.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>📍 <strong>Delay Location Tagging:</strong> Never post stories or photos with live GPS tags while you are still at the airport, school, hotel, or private residence. Post after leaving!</li>
                <li>🎫 <strong>Boarding Pass &amp; Ticket Danger:</strong> Boarding pass barcodes contain full names, passport numbers, and flight booking details. Never post photos of tickets or keys!</li>
                <li>👶 <strong>Protecting Minors &amp; Family:</strong> Avoid posting school uniforms, daily commute routines, or birth certificates that expose kids to predatory threats.</li>
                <li>🧹 <strong>Audit Past Posts:</strong> Regularly delete old posts, comments, and untag yourself from photos that disclose sensitive historical information.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="how-protect">
                <b>Action Steps:</b> Turn off camera geotagging in your phone settings. Post holiday photos after you return home to prevent home burglary risks.
            </div>
        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- SOCIAL MEDIA SAFETY SUMMARY ADVICE BOX -->
    <div class="scam-safety-box" style="margin-top: 25px;">

        <div class="scam-safety-icon">
            🛡️
        </div>

        <div>

            <h3>
                Golden Rule of Social Media Safety
            </h3>

            <p>
                "If you wouldn't paste it on a physical billboard on your city's main street, DO NOT post it online."
            </p>

            <strong>
                PAUSE → CHECK AUDIENCE → REMOVE SENSITIVE METADATA → POST SAFELY
            </strong>

        </div>

    </div>


<!-- =========================================================
     FIX: SOCIAL SECTION CLOSED HERE
     ========================================================= -->

</section>


<!-- =========================================================
     SCAM AWARENESS - UPDATED
     ========================================================= -->

<section id="awareness" class="page">

    <div class="page-title">

        <h2>
            Scam Awareness
        </h2>

        <p>
            Pause, verify and never share sensitive information under pressure.
        </p>

    </div>


    <div class="info-grid">


        <!-- DIGITAL ARREST -->

        <div class="info card scam-info-card">

            <div class="scam-image">
                <img src="images/digital-arrest.svg" alt="Digital Arrest">
            </div>

            <span class="scam-tag red">
                DIGITAL SAFETY
            </span>

            <h3>
                Digital Arrest Scam Awareness
            </h3>

            <p>
                Scammers may pretend to be police, CBI, RBI or other government officials on a video call. They create fake sets resembling police stations and create immense fear to demand money, claiming your Aadhaar or phone number is involved in illegal activities.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>❌ <strong>Fact:</strong> There is no concept of “Digital Arrest” under Indian law. Police will not arrest you over Skype or WhatsApp.</li>
                <li>📞 <strong>Action:</strong> Disconnect the video call immediately. Do not stay on the line under pressure.</li>
                <li>🔐 <strong>Security:</strong> Never transfer funds to "safe accounts" or share OTPs, passwords, or banking details.</li>
                <li>✅ <strong>Verify:</strong> Always visit your local police station or check the official portal directly.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="how-protect">
                <b>How to protect:</b>
                Stop, verify independently and do not send money because of threats. Real law enforcement does not demand money to drop charges over a call.
            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- SUSPICIOUS FILES -->

        <div class="info card scam-info-card">

            <div class="scam-image">
                <img src="images/whatsapp-boss-scam.svg" alt="Suspicious Messages">
            </div>

            <span class="scam-tag orange">
                MESSAGES &amp; FILES
            </span>

            <h3>
                Suspicious Files and Messages
            </h3>

            <p>
                Unexpected messages on WhatsApp, Telegram or SMS containing links or APK files can be used to install malware on your phone, steal banking credentials, or hijack your accounts.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>📩 <strong>Alertness:</strong> Be highly careful with unexpected messages, even if they appear to be from a friend or boss asking for urgent help.</li>
                <li>📦 <strong>Downloads:</strong> Do not download or install unknown APK files, as they bypass official app store security.</li>
                <li>🔗 <strong>Links:</strong> Avoid clicking on suspicious links offering free gifts, lottery wins, or urgent account updates.</li>
                <li>🔎 <strong>Confirm:</strong> Call the person directly on their standard phone number to confirm if they actually sent the message.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="how-protect">
                <b>How to protect:</b>
                Stop and verify the sender before opening files or clicking links. Install apps only from the official Google Play Store or Apple App Store.
            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- INVESTMENT -->

        <div class="info card scam-info-card">

            <div class="scam-image">
                <img src="images/fake-investment.svg" alt="Fake Investment">
            </div>

            <span class="scam-tag pink">
                INVESTMENT
            </span>

            <h3>
                Fake Investment Offers
            </h3>

            <p>
                Fraudsters use social media ads, messaging apps, and fake "trading groups" (often on Telegram or WhatsApp) to promote unrealistic investment returns in stocks, crypto, or forex.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>💰 <strong>Skepticism:</strong> Be highly suspicious of guaranteed or massive returns with little to no risk. If it sounds too good to be true, it is.</li>
                <li>📱 <strong>Groups:</strong> Do not trust random investment groups where everyone seems to be making huge profits (these are often fake accounts).</li>
                <li>🔐 <strong>Privacy:</strong> Never share banking details, PAN card, or login details with unverified brokers.</li>
                <li>🔎 <strong>Research:</strong> Verify that the investment platform or broker is registered with SEBI or relevant authorities.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="how-protect">
                <b>How to protect:</b>
                Research independently before making any payment or investment. Start small, and never invest money you cannot afford to lose based on a social media tip.
            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- GOVERNMENT EMAIL -->

        <div class="info card scam-info-card">

            <div class="scam-image">
                <img src="images/fake-government-mail.svg" alt="Government Email">
            </div>

            <span class="scam-tag yellow">
                FAKE GOVERNMENT EMAILS
            </span>

            <h3>
                Government Impersonation Emails
            </h3>

            <p>
                Fake emails may use official government names (like Income Tax Dept, UIDAI, Traffic Police), logos, and threatening language (e.g., "Your PAN will be blocked") to create panic.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>📧 <strong>Sender Check:</strong> Carefully examine the sender's email address. Official emails usually end in `.gov.in` or `.nic.in`, not `@gmail.com` or weird domains.</li>
                <li>⚠️ <strong>Stay Calm:</strong> Scammers use urgency to force mistakes. Do not panic because of threatening language.</li>
                <li>🔗 <strong>No Clicks:</strong> Do not blindly open links or download attachments (like fake tax refund forms) in unexpected emails.</li>
                <li>🌐 <strong>Direct Access:</strong> Instead of clicking the link, type the official government website URL directly into your browser to check your account status.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="how-protect">
                <b>How to protect:</b>
                Do not trust an official-looking logo alone. Always verify independently through official websites or customer care numbers.
            </div>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- 5 SECOND RULE -->

    <div class="scam-safety-box">

        <div class="scam-safety-icon">
            🛡️
        </div>

        <div>

            <h3>
                5-Second Safety Rule
            </h3>

            <p>
                Before clicking, paying, downloading or sharing information:
            </p>

            <strong>
                STOP → CHECK → VERIFY → THEN ACT
            </strong>

        </div>

    </div>


    <!-- REPORT -->

    <div class="scam-report-box">

        <h3>
            🚨 If you face an online financial fraud
        </h3>

        <p>
            Report cyber financial fraud immediately through the National Cyber
            Crime Reporting Portal or call the cybercrime helpline.
        </p>

        <div class="report-number">
            📞 1930
        </div>

        <small>
            National Cyber Crime Helpline
        </small>

    </div>

</section>


<!-- =========================================================
     AI & DEEPFAKE
     ========================================================= -->

<section id="ai" class="page">

    <div class="page-title">

        <h2>
            AI &amp; Deepfake Awareness
        </h2>

        <p>
            AI-generated content can look convincing. Verify before trusting or sharing.
        </p>

    </div>


    <div class="card" style="padding: 20px; margin-bottom: 25px; border-radius: 18px; overflow: hidden;">

        <div class="card-banner" style="height: 180px; margin-bottom: 20px;">

            <img
                src="images/ai-deepfake-banner.svg"
                alt="AI & Deepfake Awareness Banner"
            >

        </div>

        <h3 style="color: #24527d; font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 8px;">
            Understanding Generative AI &amp; Voice Clone Fraud
        </h3>

        <p style="color: #64839e; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6;">
            Modern AI can clone any person's voice from just a 3-second audio sample and generate hyper-realistic videos of real public figures or relatives asking for urgent money. Learn how to verify before reacting.
        </p>

    </div>


    <div class="info-grid">

        <div class="info card scam-info-card">

            <span class="scam-tag red">
                AUDIO FRAUD
            </span>

            <h3>
                AI Voice Cloning Scams
            </h3>

            <p>
                Scammers call parents or grandparents using a cloned voice of their child, crying and claiming they were arrested or in an accident and need immediate bail funds.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>🚨 <strong>Ask a Secret Question:</strong> Establish a family security passphrase that only real family members know.</li>
                <li>📞 <strong>Hang Up &amp; Call Back:</strong> Never send money immediately. Disconnect and call the family member directly on their regular phone.</li>
                <li>🤖 <strong>Listen for Unnatural Breathing:</strong> AI voices often have unnatural pacing, robotic breathing, or lack true background noise.</li>
            </ul>

        </div>


        <div class="info card scam-info-card">

            <span class="scam-tag orange">
                VIDEO MANIPULATION
            </span>

            <h3>
                Video Face Swaps &amp; Digital Arrests
            </h3>

            <p>
                Deepfake video filters are used by scammers on WhatsApp and Skype video calls to appear wearing real police uniforms or sitting inside authentic government offices.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>👀 <strong>Check Blinking &amp; Eye Movement:</strong> Many deepfakes struggle with natural eye blinking and realistic iris reflections.</li>
                <li>👤 <strong>Observe Jawlines &amp; Shadows:</strong> Watch the border of the face and neck when the speaker turns their head. Distortions or glitching indicate face swaps.</li>
                <li>✋ <strong>Request a Physical Movement:</strong> Ask the person on the video to wave their hand in front of their face. AI filters often break during rapid occlusion.</li>
            </ul>

        </div>


        <div class="info card scam-info-card">

            <span class="scam-tag pink">
                SYNTHETIC MEDIA
            </span>

            <h3>
                Fake Celebrity Endorsements
            </h3>

            <p>
                Scammers use AI to sync the lips of famous business leaders, actors, and political figures promoting get-rich-quick crypto or trading schemes on Facebook and YouTube.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>👄 <strong>Lip Sync Discrepancies:</strong> Notice if the spoken audio slightly mismatches the lip movement or syllables.</li>
                <li>🔗 <strong>Scrutinize the Website Link:</strong> Official endorsements will lead to verified brand websites, never strange third-party domains.</li>
                <li>📢 <strong>Cross-Check Legitimate News:</strong> If a celebrity made a massive investment announcement, reputable news networks would report it.</li>
            </ul>

        </div>


        <div class="info card scam-info-card">

            <span class="scam-tag yellow">
                ETHICAL DEFENSE
            </span>

            <h3>
                Stopping Misinformation &amp; Hoaxes
            </h3>

            <p>
                Viral sensational news, emergency evacuation orders, or manipulated political statements are often designed to cause social chaos and panic.
            </p>

            <ul>
                <li>⏳ <strong>The 60-Second Pause:</strong> If a video triggers intense anger, fear, or excitement, pause before hitting "Forward".</li>
                <li>🔍 <strong>Reverse Image Search:</strong> Take a screenshot of the video frame and search on Google Lens to find the original untampered video.</li>
                <li>🛡️ <strong>Fact-Checking Portals:</strong> Verify claims on official government fact-checking handles (like PIB Fact Check in India).</li>
            </ul>

        </div>

    </div>

</section>


